Phase World's 43 items, every number read off the page

Printed 114-129 is the book's personal equipment: high-intensity lasers,
Naruni plasma cartridge guns, CAF and kreeghor armour, four Naruni force
fields, promethean phase technology, gravity rail guns and the noro's psionic
crystal weapons. 22 weapon, 15 armor, 6 gear.

Fourteen pages were rendered at 200 dpi and read line by line rather than
parsed out of the OCR cache. This section prices in five and six figures and
BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT F1 is exactly about these columns - nothing anywhere checks a
numeric value against the page it cites - so a misread digit here is an order of
magnitude and invisible afterwards. The OCR turned out to agree everywhere: zero
discrepancies across 43 stat blocks. That is a fact about this cache, not an
argument for skipping the check next time; the reason to render is that the
error would be silent, and that holds whether or not one was there.

The `^Cost:` scan of the cache finds 36 of 43 prices and misses every one on
printed 119-122, because the label is written "Black Market Cost:" and wraps
across a line break in the narrow columns. Anything re-parsing this section has
to join lines first.

Force fields and phase fields are filed 'armor' rather than 'gear', which is a
first for this catalog - it holds no force fields today. The book's own rule on
printed 121 decides it: a force field cannot be worn over armour unless it is
built into the armour, so it is not an accessory to protection, it IS the
protection, and its M.D.C. belongs where the sheet's armour block reads M.D.C.
from. Helmets go the other way, following the catalog's existing pas-helmet:
a helmet is worn WITH body armour and filing it as armour would double-count.

The Naruni items price three ways - personal, integral, and a robot model at
twenty times the integral - and nine weapons price their ammunition separately
from the gun. `cost` always holds the first of those, the one a character
actually buys; everything else is in `cost_note`. The readback asserts zero
rows with a NULL cost, because this book sells everything and a missing price
here would be a failed read rather than a fact about the book, the way
Wormwood's barter economy was.

No vessels. Printed 130-149 and 157-173 carry 6 power armor and robots, 5 tanks
and 14 starships, and `gear` has one mdc, one damage, one range and one payload
against a stat block with M.D.C. by location, five to eight numbered weapon
systems, crew and passenger complements and FTL range in light years per hour.
Storing one means keeping one weapon out of eight and dropping the rest, and the
row would then read as complete. BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT F3, which also records that
this is not new with this book - the catalog's existing robot rows lose the same
data silently.

Applied --remote before this commit. Catalog is 1018 gear rows.
